### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or rotation angle to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;          /* card width */
    height:360px;         /* card height */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hint that it's interactive */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper (the rotating part) ---------- */
.card-inner {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front side of the card ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
}

/* Front styling */
.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Back styling */
.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* start rotated so it's hidden */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* flip the card */
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Optional: Add some content styles ---------- */
.card h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
}
.card p {
    margin:0;
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#555;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Here is the other side.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives depth to the 3D rotation. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility:hidden` on both sides | Hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | On hover, `.card-inner` rotates 180° around Y-axis | Creates the flip effect. |
| 5 | The back side is initially rotated 180° so it starts hidden | When the parent rotates, the back becomes visible. |

Feel free to replace the placeholder text, add images, or tweak the colors. If you want a different rotation axis (e.g., X‑axis for a vertical flip), change `rotateY` to `rotateX`. Enjoy!
